Project Title
Quality Assurance Portfolio: Selenium Automation with Java

Description
This repository serves as a portfolio of my work in Quality Assurance and automated software testing. It focuses on using the Selenium WebDriver framework in conjunction with Java to create robust and maintainable test automation scripts. The projects within this repository demonstrate my proficiency in key testing concepts and practices, including:

Test Case Design: Creating comprehensive and effective test cases.

Test Automation: Implementing automated tests for web applications using Selenium and Java.

Page Object Model (POM): Applying the POM design pattern for creating reusable and organized test code.

Framework Development: Building a scalable and easy-to-manage test automation framework.

CI/CD Integration: Demonstrating knowledge of integrating automation tests into a continuous integration/continuous deployment pipeline.

This portfolio is a showcase of my skills and a practical example of my ability to contribute to the quality of software development.

Technologies Used
Java: The core programming language for the automation scripts.

Selenium WebDriver: The primary tool for automating web browser interactions.

JUnit/TestNG: The testing framework used to structure and run tests.

Maven/Gradle: Build automation tools for managing project dependencies and compiling code.

